# Gantry — The game's state

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The game's whole state lives in one value: the one the frame loop advances and
the debug surface (`specs/instrumentation.md`) poses and reads. Its shape is
yours to design, and this file states what it must carry, because the rest of
the specification and the snapshot in `specs/instrumentation.md` are written
against these facts.
{{else}}
The game's whole state is `GantryState`, declared and exported from
`src/game.ts` exactly as below, together with the types it is built from. The
engine holds the state by value: `update` and the debug surface's poses take a
read-only view and return the next state, so nothing ever writes into a held
one. The comments are part of the declaration's meaning; carry them into the
build.

```ts
/** A position, in world units; lattice positions carry lattice coordinates. */
export interface Vec3 {
  x: number;
  y: number;
  z: number;
}

export type MaterialName = "strut" | "cable" | "rail";

/** One member. `id` is unique for the life of a site's structure. */
export interface Member {
  id: number;
  a: Vec3;
  b: Vec3;
  material: MaterialName;
}

/** What the player has built on the current site. */
export interface Structure {
  members: Member[];
  /** The next member id to assign; never reused within a site. */
  nextMemberId: number;
  /** The slew ring, by its base corner (specs/structure.md), or none yet. */
  ring: { corner: Vec3 } | null;
  /** The nodes carrying a counterweight. */
  counterweights: Vec3[];
}

export type AxisName = "slew" | "trolley" | "hoist" | "grip";

export interface Command {
  axis: AxisName;
  target: number;
  rate: number;
}

/** One tape step: a move of one or more axes, or an action. */
export type Step =
  | { kind: "move"; commands: Command[] }
  | { kind: "action"; action: "attach" | "release" };

/** One axis during a run. `command` is null when no command is live on it. */
export interface AxisState {
  value: number;
  rate: number;
  command: { target: number; rate: number } | null;
}

export type LoadPhase = "waiting" | "attached" | "placed" | "lost";

/** One load during a run, index-aligned with the site's load list. */
export interface LoadState {
  phase: LoadPhase;
  /** The lift point's current position (specs/world.md). */
  pos: Vec3;
  yaw: number;
}

export type RunPhase = "idle" | "running" | "cleared" | "failed";

export type FailCause =
  | "collapse"
  | "ring-overload"
  | "cable-snap"
  | "structure-struck-obstacle"
  | "load-struck-obstacle"
  | "load-struck-ground"
  | "attach-missed"
  | "release-misplaced"
  | "command-out-of-range"
  | "loads-unplaced";

/** The run in progress, or the idle placeholder between runs. */
export interface RunState {
  phase: RunPhase;
  /** The failure cause; null unless phase is "failed". */
  cause: FailCause | null;
  /** Ticks since the run started; the run clock is tick / TICK_HZ. */
  tick: number;
  /** Index into RUN_SPEEDS. */
  speedIndex: number;
  /** The index of the live tape step; the tape's length once all are done. */
  stepIndex: number;
  axes: { slew: AxisState; trolley: AxisState; hoist: AxisState; grip: AxisState };
  /** The pendulum bob: the hook point (specs/rigging.md). */
  bob: { pos: Vec3; vel: Vec3 };
  /** The attached load's index, or null. */
  attached: number | null;
  loads: LoadState[];
  /** The latest solve's force and utilization per intact member. */
  forces: { id: number; force: number; utilization: number }[];
  /** The ids of members broken so far this run. */
  broken: number[];
}

/** A cleared site's recorded score. */
export interface Score {
  cost: number;
  time: number;
}

/** The orbit camera (specs/controls.md). */
export interface Camera {
  yaw: number;
  pitch: number;
  dist: number;
}

export type Screen =
  | "title"
  | "howto"
  | "select"
  | "build"
  | "program"
  | "run"
  | "results";

export type Tool =
  | "strut"
  | "cable"
  | "rail"
  | "ring"
  | "counterweight"
  | "delete";

export interface GantryState {
  screen: Screen;
  /** The highlighted item of the current screen's menu. */
  menuIndex: number;
  /** The open (or last open) site, counted from 0. */
  siteIndex: number;
  /** Per site: whether it has ever been cleared this session. */
  cleared: boolean[];
  /** Per site: the best recorded score, or null before the first clear. */
  best: (Score | null)[];
  /** Per site: the authored structure and tape, persisting across visits. */
  sites: { structure: Structure; program: Step[] }[];
  /** The selected build tool. */
  tool: Tool;
  /** The held first node of a member placement, or null. */
  pendingNode: Vec3 | null;
  /**
   * The undo stack for the open site: the structure as it was before each
   * structure-changing edit since the site was opened, oldest first.
   */
  history: Structure[];
  camera: Camera;
  run: RunState;
  /** The runtime's mute bit, mirrored every update. */
  muted: boolean;
  /** Accumulated delta time of every update, in seconds. */
  simTime: number;
}
```
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
## What the state carries

- The current screen, one of `title`, `howto`, `select`, `build`, `program`,
  `run`, or `results`, and the highlighted index of that screen's menu.
- The open site's index, and per site: whether it has ever been cleared this
  session, the best recorded score (`cost` and `time`, or none before the
  first clear), and the authored structure and tape, persisting across visits
  within the session.
- A structure: its members, each carrying an id unique for the life of the
  site's structure, its two lattice nodes, and its material; the ring by its
  base corner, or none; and the counterweight nodes.
- The tape: the ordered steps, each a move of per-axis commands or an
  `attach`/`release` action.
- The build screen's tool, the pending first node of a member placement, and
  the undo history for the open site.
- The camera's yaw, pitch, and distance.
- The run: its phase (`idle`, `running`, `cleared`, `failed`) and failure
  cause; the tick count; the watch-speed index; the live step index; each
  axis's value, rate, and live command; the pendulum bob's position and
  velocity; the attached load's index; each load's phase (`waiting`,
  `attached`, `placed`, `lost`), lift-point position, and yaw; the latest
  solve's force and utilization per intact member; and the ids of members
  broken this run.
- `muted`, mirroring the runtime's mute bit, and `simTime`, accumulating every
  update's delta time in seconds.

The failure causes are the fixed vocabulary `specs/statics.md` closes with.
Anything else a frame needs is derivable from these facts.
{{else}}
## How it advances

`initialize` builds the complete initial state: the title screen with
`menuIndex` `0`, every site's `cleared` false, `best` null, and empty
structure and tape, the strut tool, no pending node, the camera at its start
pose, an idle run, `muted` mirroring the engine, and `simTime` `0`. The idle
`RunState` carries `phase` `"idle"`, `cause` null, zeroed tick and indices,
the axes at the run-start posture (`specs/program.md`) with no command, the
bob at rest, no attachment, an empty `loads`, `forces`, and `broken`.

Opening a site sets `siteIndex`, keeps that site's stored structure and tape,
clears `history` and `pendingNode`, resets the camera to its start pose, and
leaves the run idle. Every figure a frame needs beyond these fields is
derived: the cost from the structure, the track from the rail members, the
world geometry from the slew angle, and the readiness issues from the rules in
`specs/structure.md`.
{{/if}}
